{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvKHGdxmuWrHwzQ4gkp4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`vitest --repeats=<n>` runs every test `n` extra times, whether it passes or fails. The default is `0`. If any one of those runs fails, the whole test is marked as failed, so the flag is mainly for finding flaky tests. A test that sets its own `repeats` option (e.g. `test('x', { repeats: 3 }, ...)`) overrides the global value. `--retry` is different: it only re-runs a test after it fails, and the test passes if any attempt succeeds.\n\nI found the flag documented only on the config page for Vitest's main branch, not in the CLI reference. It may be new, so check that your installed version supports it.\n\nSources:\n- [Vitest config: repeats (main.vitest.dev)](https://main.vitest.dev/config/repeats)\n- [docs/config/repeats.md mirror](https://next.tangled.org/vitest.dev/vitest/blob/main/docs/config/repeats.md)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":915,"cache_read_input_tokens":22346,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":915},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e844aed-6d69-40c2-80d7-902479bbb6e1","uuid":"3295bac6-c8de-45fd-be71-a4276fdbd9a2","timestamp":"2026-10-11T10:46:43.440Z","request_id":"req_011CfvKHGPL2e4gekbzZwD2N"}
